/P 200 0 R
/E (Lei Lei is Professor of Applied Linguistics at Shanghai International Studies University. His research uses corpus and NLP methods to study lexical and syntactic patterns in Modern Chinese, Classical Chinese, and English. He also works on second-language writing and digital humanities. He has authored five books and more than fifty international journal articles, led two projects funded by the China National Social Science Fund, and serves in editorial roles for journals in academic writing and corpus-based humanities.)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [11]
>>
