434 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 205 0 R
/T (Speech-based Alzheimer's disease \(AD\) detection offers a non-invasive route to cognitive screening, but most available resources remain concentrated in English, limiting deployment in low-resource languages. We address cross-lingual AD detection on the ADReSS-M benchmark, where models trained mainly on English spontaneous speech must generalize to Greek with limited target-language supervision. We propose a transcript-free two-stage framework in which a pretrained Wav2 Vec2 encoder is fine-tuned on English speech with a lightweight prosodic branch, and the resulting attention-pooled acoustic embeddings are adapted to Greek through an attention-based classifier with mixed-batch few-shot transfer. Across five random seeds, the proposed framework achieved Greek test accuracies ranging from 73.68% to 84.21%, with the best model reaching 84.21% accuracy and 83.33% F1-score. These results suggest that supervised acoustic embedding transfer is a promising direction for cross-lingual transcript-free AD detection.)
/E (Speech-based Alzheimer's disease \(AD\) detection offers a non-invasive route to cognitive screening, but most available resources remain concentrated in English, limiting deployment in low-resource languages. We address cross-lingual AD detection on the ADReSS-M benchmark, where models trained mainly on English spontaneous speech must generalize to Greek with limited target-language supervision. We propose a transcript-free two-stage framework in which a pretrained Wav2 Vec2 encoder is fine-tuned on English speech with a lightweight prosodic branch, and the resulting attention-pooled acoustic embeddings are adapted to Greek through an attention-based classifier with mixed-batch few-shot transfer. Across five random seeds, the proposed framework achieved Greek test accuracies ranging from 73.68% to 84.21%, with the best model reaching 84.21% accuracy and 83.33% F1-score. These results suggest that supervised acoustic embedding transfer is a promising direction for cross-lingual transcript-free AD detection.)
/Pg 23 0 R
/K [11]
>>
endobj
