461 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 207 0 R
/T (Feminist literary research has transformed to digital qualitative methods to strengthen interpretive rigor without sacrificing textual sensitivity. Our study focused on comparative corpus-assisted thematic analysis of two landmark feminist poetry collections from South Asia-Kishwar Naheed's Compositions of a Scorched Heart and Meena Kandasamy's Ms. Militancy. We employed NVivo as a computer-assisted qualitative data analysis software \(CAQDAS\) to systematically code feminist themes across the two corpora, focusing on gender identity, patriarchy, empowerment, resistance, and sisterhood.)
/E (Feminist literary research has transformed to digital qualitative methods to strengthen interpretive rigor without sacrificing textual sensitivity. Our study focused on comparative corpus-assisted thematic analysis of two landmark feminist poetry collections from South Asia-Kishwar Naheed's Compositions of a Scorched Heart and Meena Kandasamy's Ms. Militancy. We employed NVivo as a computer-assisted qualitative data analysis software \(CAQDAS\) to systematically code feminist themes across the two corpora, focusing on gender identity, patriarchy, empowerment, resistance, and sisterhood.)
/Pg 25 0 R
/K [10]
>>
endobj
462 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 207 0 R
/T (We conducted qualitative thematic coding, sentiment distribution, and cross-corpus comparison on selected works grounded in feminist theory and qualitative rigor. Our results suggest both convergence and divergence in feminist articulation. Naheed's work demonstrated relational feminist ethos rooted in collective solidarity, whereas Kandasamy's poetry articulates a confrontational feminist politics shaped by caste and militant resistance. We demonstrated how stylistic structures serve as both aesthetic and political instruments to analyse feminist discourse using the CAQDAS method in literary research.)
/E (We conducted qualitative thematic coding, sentiment distribution, and cross-corpus comparison on selected works grounded in feminist theory and qualitative rigor. Our results suggest both convergence and divergence in feminist articulation. Naheed's work demonstrated relational feminist ethos rooted in collective solidarity, whereas Kandasamy's poetry articulates a confrontational feminist politics shaped by caste and militant resistance. We demonstrated how stylistic structures serve as both aesthetic and political instruments to analyse feminist discourse using the CAQDAS method in literary research.)
/Pg 25 0 R
/K [11]
>>
endobj
