525 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 211 0 R
/T (This study makes three significant contributions to corpus linguistics and language pedagogy. First, it demonstrates that specialized corpora can serve as accessible reference tools for non-linguist students when pedagogically scaffolded, challenging assumptions that corpus applications require extensive linguistic training. Second, it provides empirical evidence that corpus consultation addresses terminological asymmetries between source and target languages, a critical need in rapidly evolving technical domains where lexical gaps require informed term creation. Third, the findings reveal that guided corpus exploration cultivates critical awareness of automated translation limitations, fostering analytical skills transferable beyond the classroom. For practitioners, this research offers working strategies for integrating specialized corpora into ESP curricula, while for corpus linguists, it underscores the importance of user-centered design in expanding corpus applications beyond traditional linguistic research contexts.)
/E (This study makes three significant contributions to corpus linguistics and language pedagogy. First, it demonstrates that specialized corpora can serve as accessible reference tools for non-linguist students when pedagogically scaffolded, challenging assumptions that corpus applications require extensive linguistic training. Second, it provides empirical evidence that corpus consultation addresses terminological asymmetries between source and target languages, a critical need in rapidly evolving technical domains where lexical gaps require informed term creation. Third, the findings reveal that guided corpus exploration cultivates critical awareness of automated translation limitations, fostering analytical skills transferable beyond the classroom. For practitioners, this research offers working strategies for integrating specialized corpora into ESP curricula, while for corpus linguists, it underscores the importance of user-centered design in expanding corpus applications beyond traditional linguistic research contexts.)
/Pg 29 0 R
/K [10]
>>
endobj
