/S /H2
/P 213 0 R
/T (Conducted in an ELT setting, this study aims to explore ELT students' translation practices regarding culture-specific expressions. Given that culture-specific translations require due attention because idioms or culturally bound phrases are rooted in social, context-specific, and real-life experiences, it is profoundly significant to shed light on learners' translations of cultural expressions by scrutinizing common errors, recurring patterns, and difficulty levels. Accordingly, in this study, a sample of ELT students was asked to translate a text including cultural elements. Then, culture-specific translations were compiled into a small-scale learner corpus and analyzed both quantitatively and qualitatively. The analysis findings were used as sources to develop a learner corpus, especially for translation training.)
/E (Conducted in an ELT setting, this study aims to explore ELT students' translation practices regarding culture-specific expressions. Given that culture-specific translations require due attention because idioms or culturally bound phrases are rooted in social, context-specific, and real-life experiences, it is profoundly significant to shed light on learners' translations of cultural expressions by scrutinizing common errors, recurring patterns, and difficulty levels. Accordingly, in this study, a sample of ELT students was asked to translate a text including cultural elements. Then, culture-specific translations were compiled into a small-scale learner corpus and analyzed both quantitatively and qualitatively. The analysis findings were used as sources to develop a learner corpus, especially for translation training.)
/Pg 31 0 R
/K [12]
>>
endobj
