/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 217 0 R
/T (The increasing globalization of professional communication places translators at the intersection of languages and cultures, requiring them to navigate not only linguistic structures but also intercultural nuances. This paper examines the role of corpus technology in translator education, focusing on its potential to enhance intercultural communication competence. Corpora provide access to authentic, large-scale language data, enabling learners to observe recurrent discourse patterns, pragmatic conventions, and culturally embedded communicative strategies. By engaging with corpus-driven tasks, students are encouraged to move beyond surface-level translation and develop sensitivity to cultural variation in meaning, register, and rhetorical organization.)
/E (The increasing globalization of professional communication places translators at the intersection of languages and cultures, requiring them to navigate not only linguistic structures but also intercultural nuances. This paper examines the role of corpus technology in translator education, focusing on its potential to enhance intercultural communication competence. Corpora provide access to authentic, large-scale language data, enabling learners to observe recurrent discourse patterns, pragmatic conventions, and culturally embedded communicative strategies. By engaging with corpus-driven tasks, students are encouraged to move beyond surface-level translation and develop sensitivity to cultural variation in meaning, register, and rhetorical organization.)
/Pg 35 0 R
/K [11]
>>
endobj
623 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 217 0 R
/T (The study outlines pedagogical approaches that integrate corpus tools into classroom practice, including comparative analysis of parallel corpora, exploration of collocational norms, and investigation of genre-specific discourse. These activities allow future translators to identify divergences between source and target language conventions, fostering awareness of how cultural values and communicative traditions shape textual production. The paper also highlights the transformative potential of error analysis when mediated through corpora: rather than being viewed as isolated mistakes, errors become gateways to deeper insights into intercultural differences.)
/E (The study outlines pedagogical approaches that integrate corpus tools into classroom practice, including comparative analysis of parallel corpora, exploration of collocational norms, and investigation of genre-specific discourse. These activities allow future translators to identify divergences between source and target language conventions, fostering awareness of how cultural values and communicative traditions shape textual production. The paper also highlights the transformative potential of error analysis when mediated through corpora: rather than being viewed as isolated mistakes, errors become gateways to deeper insights into intercultural differences.)
/Pg 35 0 R
/K [12]
>>
endobj
624 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 217 0 R
/T (Practical examples illustrate how corpus-based exercises can be embedded into translator training modules, equipping students with analytical strategies that strengthen both linguistic precision and intercultural adaptability. The findings suggest that corpus technology serves as a bridge between theoretical knowledge and professional practice, cultivating translators who are not only accurate but also culturally responsive. Ultimately, the integration of corpora into translator education contributes to the development of professionals capable of mediating across cultures with clarity, sensitivity, and confidence.)
/E (Practical examples illustrate how corpus-based exercises can be embedded into translator training modules, equipping students with analytical strategies that strengthen both linguistic precision and intercultural adaptability. The findings suggest that corpus technology serves as a bridge between theoretical knowledge and professional practice, cultivating translators who are not only accurate but also culturally responsive. Ultimately, the integration of corpora into translator education contributes to the development of professionals capable of mediating across cultures with clarity, sensitivity, and confidence.)
/Pg 35 0 R
/K [13]
>>
endobj
