654 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 219 0 R
/T (In contemporary translation studies, sociolinguistic competence is considered a crucial component of professional translator training, as translators must understand not only linguistic structures but also sociocultural patterns of language use. This study explores the development of sociolinguistic competence among future translators through a gender-oriented pedagogical approach supported by corpus linguistics. In particular, the research utilizes the Corpus of Contemporary American English \(COCA\) as a corpus-based resource for analyzing gender-related language patterns and discourse practices.)
/E (In contemporary translation studies, sociolinguistic competence is considered a crucial component of professional translator training, as translators must understand not only linguistic structures but also sociocultural patterns of language use. This study explores the development of sociolinguistic competence among future translators through a gender-oriented pedagogical approach supported by corpus linguistics. In particular, the research utilizes the Corpus of Contemporary American English \(COCA\) as a corpus-based resource for analyzing gender-related language patterns and discourse practices.)
/Pg 37 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
655 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 219 0 R
/T (The study aims to design and evaluate a corpus-informed instructional model that integrates gender-sensitive analysis into translator education. The research methodology combines theoretical analysis, corpus-based linguistic investigation, curriculum analysis, classroom observation, surveys, and pedagogical experimentation. Using the COCA corpus, students were engaged in data-driven learning activities that involved identifying gender-marked lexical choices, discourse strategies, and pragmatic features in authentic texts across different registers.)
/E (The study aims to design and evaluate a corpus-informed instructional model that integrates gender-sensitive analysis into translator education. The research methodology combines theoretical analysis, corpus-based linguistic investigation, curriculum analysis, classroom observation, surveys, and pedagogical experimentation. Using the COCA corpus, students were engaged in data-driven learning activities that involved identifying gender-marked lexical choices, discourse strategies, and pragmatic features in authentic texts across different registers.)
/Pg 37 0 R
/K [10]
>>
endobj
656 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 219 0 R
/T (The results of the pedagogical experiment demonstrate that corpus-assisted instruction significantly improves students' ability to recognize gendered language patterns, interpret sociolinguistic variation, and produce culturally appropriate translations. The findings suggest that integrating corpus linguistics with gender-oriented pedagogy enhances critical linguistic awareness and strengthens sociolinguistic competence in translator training.)
/E (The results of the pedagogical experiment demonstrate that corpus-assisted instruction significantly improves students' ability to recognize gendered language patterns, interpret sociolinguistic variation, and produce culturally appropriate translations. The findings suggest that integrating corpus linguistics with gender-oriented pedagogy enhances critical linguistic awareness and strengthens sociolinguistic competence in translator training.)
/Pg 37 0 R
/K [11]
>>
endobj
657 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 219 0 R
/T (The study concludes that corpus-based approaches, particularly those utilizing large authentic corpora such as COCA, provide effective methodological tools for developing sociolinguistic and intercultural competence in future translators.)
/E (The study concludes that corpus-based approaches, particularly those utilizing large authentic corpora such as COCA, provide effective methodological tools for developing sociolinguistic and intercultural competence in future translators.)
/Pg 37 0 R
/K [12]
