724 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 223 0 R
/T (Natural Language Processing \(NLP\) is an important field that develops computers' ability to understand, interpret, and process human language. One of its key directions, sentiment analysis, focuses on identifying the emotional tone expressed in texts. Through sentiment analysis, texts are classified into positive, negative, or neutral categories. The main objective of sentiment analysis is to automatically interpret human opinions. The growing volume of textual data such as social media posts, reviews, discussions, and news has significantly increased the importance of this field. In modern times, companies widely use sentiment analysis to measure customer satisfaction, analyze user behavior, and identify market trends.)
/E (Natural Language Processing \(NLP\) is an important field that develops computers' ability to understand, interpret, and process human language. One of its key directions, sentiment analysis, focuses on identifying the emotional tone expressed in texts. Through sentiment analysis, texts are classified into positive, negative, or neutral categories. The main objective of sentiment analysis is to automatically interpret human opinions. The growing volume of textual data such as social media posts, reviews, discussions, and news has significantly increased the importance of this field. In modern times, companies widely use sentiment analysis to measure customer satisfaction, analyze user behavior, and identify market trends.)
/Pg 41 0 R
/K [11]
>>
endobj
725 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 223 0 R
/T (The approaches used in this field are generally divided into two main groups: lexicon-based and machine learning-based methods. In the lexicon-based approach, predefined emotional word dictionaries are utilized. Each word is assigned a specific emotional value, and the overall tone of the text is determined based on the sum of these values. On the other hand, machine learning approaches rely on models trained on large volumes of labeled data. These models detect hidden patterns in texts and enable more accurate results. In recent years, the development of deep learning methods has significantly improved the quality of sentiment analysis. Neural networks, particularly recurrent neural networks \(RNNs\), long short-term memory \(LSTM\) models, and transformers, help better understand the context of text. These technologies allow for more precise analysis not only at the word level but also at the sentence and discourse levels.)
/E (The approaches used in this field are generally divided into two main groups: lexicon-based and machine learning-based methods. In the lexicon-based approach, predefined emotional word dictionaries are utilized. Each word is assigned a specific emotional value, and the overall tone of the text is determined based on the sum of these values. On the other hand, machine learning approaches rely on models trained on large volumes of labeled data. These models detect hidden patterns in texts and enable more accurate results. In recent years, the development of deep learning methods has significantly improved the quality of sentiment analysis. Neural networks, particularly recurrent neural networks \(RNNs\), long short-term memory \(LSTM\) models, and transformers, help better understand the context of text. These technologies allow for more precise analysis not only at the word level but also at the sentence and discourse levels.)
/Pg 41 0 R
/K [12]
>>
endobj
726 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 223 0 R
/T (However, sentiment analysis still faces certain challenges. The complexity of language, ambiguity, sarcasm, and irony make the analysis process difficult. For instance, the same word may express different emotional meanings depending on the context. Additionally, differences between languages and cultures affect the generalization capability of models. In conclusion, sentiment analysis is a crucial branch of NLP with wide applications in both theoretical and practical domains. With further advancements in this field, more accurate and context-aware analyses will become possible, contributing to more effective human-computer interaction.)
/E (However, sentiment analysis still faces certain challenges. The complexity of language, ambiguity, sarcasm, and irony make the analysis process difficult. For instance, the same word may express different emotional meanings depending on the context. Additionally, differences between languages and cultures affect the generalization capability of models. In conclusion, sentiment analysis is a crucial branch of NLP with wide applications in both theoretical and practical domains. With further advancements in this field, more accurate and context-aware analyses will become possible, contributing to more effective human-computer interaction.)
/Pg 41 0 R
/K [13]
>>
endobj
727 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H5
