/Title (However, sentiment analysis still faces certain challenges. The complexity of language, ambiguity, sarcasm, and irony make the analysis process difficult. For instance, the same word may express different emotional meanings depending on the context. Additionally, differences between languages and cultures affect the generalization capability of models. In conclusion, sentiment analysis is a crucial branch of NLP with wide applications in both theoretical and practical domains. With further advancements in this field, more accurate and context-aware analyses will become possible, contributing to more effective human-computer interaction.)
/Dest [41 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 1835 0 R
/Prev 2358 0 R
/First 2359 0 R
