/Title (The approaches used in this field are generally divided into two main groups: lexicon-based and machine learning-based methods. In the lexicon-based approach, predefined emotional word dictionaries are utilized. Each word is assigned a specific emotional value, and the overall tone of the text is determined based on the sum of these values. On the other hand, machine learning approaches rely on models trained on large volumes of labeled data. These models detect hidden patterns in texts and enable more accurate results. In recent years, the development of deep learning methods has significantly improved the quality of sentiment analysis. Neural networks, particularly recurrent neural networks \(RNNs\), long short-term memory \(LSTM\) models, and transformers, help better understand the context of text. These technologies allow for more precise analysis not only at the word level but also at the sentence and discourse levels.)
