/Title (We conducted qualitative thematic coding, sentiment distribution, and cross-corpus comparison on selected works grounded in feminist theory and qualitative rigor. Our results suggest both convergence and divergence in feminist articulation. Naheed's work demonstrated relational feminist ethos rooted in collective solidarity, whereas Kandasamy's poetry articulates a confrontational feminist politics shaped by caste and militant resistance. We demonstrated how stylistic structures serve as both aesthetic and political instruments to analyse feminist discourse using the CAQDAS method in literary research.)
/Dest [25 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 2354 0 R
/Prev 2526 0 R
/First 2527 0 R
/Last 2528 0 R
/Count -2
>>
