2526 0 obj
<<
/Title (Feminist literary research has transformed to digital qualitative methods to strengthen interpretive rigor without sacrificing textual sensitivity. Our study focused on comparative corpus-assisted thematic analysis of two landmark feminist poetry collections from South Asia-Kishwar Naheed's Compositions of a Scorched Heart and Meena Kandasamy's Ms. Militancy. We employed NVivo as a computer-assisted qualitative data analysis software \(CAQDAS\) to systematically code feminist themes across the two corpora, focusing on gender identity, patriarchy, empowerment, resistance, and sisterhood.)
/Dest [25 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 2354 0 R
/Prev 2542 0 R
/Next 2503 0 R
>>
