/Title (Building communication during an emergency has become an increasingly important and global concern in today's rapidly changing world. To ensure public and environmental safety in an emergency, clear, understandable, and effective communication should be established between rescue teams and individuals. As a fundamental requirement for such communications, people should be equipped with essential, relevant, and situation-specific vocabulary. Lexical knowledge of emergency-related vocabulary can be enhanced through using corpus-based data. However, the literature notes the scarcity of studies on emergency-specific vocabulary.)
