/Title (This study examines the adoption of artificial intelligence \(AI\) in teaching through the lens of the Technology Acceptance Model \(TAM\), focusing on how perceived usefulness and perceived ease of use shape educators' intentions to integrate AI-driven tools into instructional practices. As AI becomes increasingly embedded in pedagogy, its psychological impacts, ranging from increased confidence and reduced workload to anxiety, uncertainty, and concerns over professional identity, have become critical considerations.)
