/Title (Methodologically, the study employs descriptive analysis, structural-semantic approaches, corpus annotation techniques, and SQL-based database modeling. The concordances were implemented using Microsoft SQL Server as the database management system, with Microsoft SQL Server Management Studio \(SSMS\) employed for data structuring, querying, and concordance generation. Particular attention is given to the development of concordances derived from the corpus data. The concordance system allows for the extraction of all contextual occurrences of a given lexical item, providing a powerful tool for analyzing lexical, semantic, and discourse-level patterns.The results indicate that the constructed corpus and its concordance outputs serve as an effective resource for linguistic research. They enable frequency analysis, lexical studies, discourse analysis, and applications in natural language processing \(NLP\). Moreover, the structured nature of the database facilitates scalability and integration with artificial intelligence systems. In conclusion, the proposed corpus model and concordance system contribute significantly to the digital representation of the Azerbaijani language and provide a solid foundation for future developments in corpus linguistics and language technologies.)
/Dest [28 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 2549 0 R
/Prev 2574 0 R
/First 2575 0 R
/Last 2576 0 R
/Count -2
>>
endobj
