/Title (Findings are expected to show that corpus use increases translation awareness, but tool difficulties and extra resource needs may affect learning. In conclusion, ad hoc corpora are considered effective pedagogical tools that complement existing practices in translation education. This study aims to fill the gap in the literature regarding the pedagogical potential of ad hoc corpus use by providing empirical data on the implementation of corpus-assisted translation teaching at the undergraduate level.)
