/Title (The study outlines pedagogical approaches that integrate corpus tools into classroom practice, including comparative analysis of parallel corpora, exploration of collocational norms, and investigation of genre-specific discourse. These activities allow future translators to identify divergences between source and target language conventions, fostering awareness of how cultural values and communicative traditions shape textual production. The paper also highlights the transformative potential of error analysis when mediated through corpora: rather than being viewed as isolated mistakes, errors become gateways to deeper insights into intercultural differences.)
