/Title (The findings reveal clear cross-disciplinary differences. Titles in the soft sciences \(Linguistics and Political Science\) tend to exhibit greater syntactic complexity and variation, frequently incorporating multi-part constructions, interrogatives, and occasionally metaphorical or allusive elements. In contrast, titles in the hard sciences \(Genetics and Condensed Matter Physics\) are typically more informationally dense, favoring compact nominal structures. These differences reflect broader epistemic orientations: interpretive disciplines appear to allow greater rhetorical flexibility, whereas experimental sciences prioritize precision and terminological specificity.)
/Dest [30 0 R /Fit]
