/Title (In the case of Uzbek translations of UN documents, the research identifies several recurring challenges, including inconsistencies in rendering key institutional terms, variation in syntactic structures, and the influence of intermediary languages such as Russian. The study demonstrates that a corpus-based approach allows for the detection of these inconsistencies and supports the development of standardized terminological databases and translation guidelines. Furthermore, the integration of corpus tools with expert validation enhances both the reliability and reproducibility of terminological decisions.)
