/Title (The increasing globalization of professional communication places translators at the intersection of languages and cultures, requiring them to navigate not only linguistic structures but also intercultural nuances. This paper examines the role of corpus technology in translator education, focusing on its potential to enhance intercultural communication competence. Corpora provide access to authentic, large-scale language data, enabling learners to observe recurrent discourse patterns, pragmatic conventions, and culturally embedded communicative strategies. By engaging with corpus-driven tasks, students are encouraged to move beyond surface-level translation and develop sensitivity to cultural variation in meaning, register, and rhetorical organization.)
/Dest [35 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 2563 0 R
/Prev 2622 0 R
