/Title (Conducted in an ELT setting, this study aims to explore ELT students' translation practices regarding culture-specific expressions. Given that culture-specific translations require due attention because idioms or culturally bound phrases are rooted in social, context-specific, and real-life experiences, it is profoundly significant to shed light on learners' translations of cultural expressions by scrutinizing common errors, recurring patterns, and difficulty levels. Accordingly, in this study, a sample of ELT students was asked to translate a text including cultural elements. Then, culture-specific translations were compiled into a small-scale learner corpus and analyzed both quantitatively and qualitatively. The analysis findings were used as sources to develop a learner corpus, especially for translation training.)
/Dest [31 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 2598 0 R
/Prev 2643 0 R
/Next 2616 0 R
