/Title (The study proposes a multi-level framework for terminological alignment that integrates linguistic, cognitive, and corpus-driven approaches. At the macro level, alignment is achieved through the identification of domain-specific conceptual structures and their standardized representation across languages. At the micro level, the methodology involves sentence-level and term-level alignment using concordance tools, frequency analysis, and context-sensitive mapping of equivalents. Special emphasis is placed on resolving issues of non-equivalence, polysemy, and culturally bound terms through strategies such as borrowing, calquing, descriptive translation, and functional adaptation.)
/Dest [34 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 2580 0 R
/Prev 2648 0 R
