/Title (Terminological consistency in multilingual institutional discourse remains a critical challenge, particularly in the context of United Nations \(UN\) documentation, where semantic precision directly affects legal interpretation, policy implementation, and cross-cultural communication. This study explores the principles and practices of terminological alignment in UN documents through the lens of parallel corpus methodology, with special attention to Uzbek-language translations. The research is grounded in a specially compiled parallel corpus consisting of aligned UN texts in English and Uzbek, enabling systematic comparison of lexical, semantic, and pragmatic features across languages.)
