/Title (Summary of findings/results \(preliminary\): Preliminary results suggest that OCR noise is patterned rather than random and that a limited number of recurring classes account for most high-impact distortions across the sample. Class-targeted preprocessing appears to offer a more methodologically stable alternative than undifferentiated cleaning, reducing persistent non-lexical artifacts and improving the interpretability of frequency-based and phraseological outputs.)
/Dest [32 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 2617 0 R
/Prev 2656 0 R
/Next 2646 0 R
>>
